abstract: >-
  Unpublished candidate metadata for the code, pre-declarations, provenance
  manifests, and evaluation artifacts accompanying a narrow modular study of a
  gradient-active left-causal depthwise FIR residual in an HSTU-style sequential
  recommender. The fail-closed graph recomputes 192 active paper cells across 18
  families and preserves null, deviated, and VOID outcomes. The evidence does not
  support broad SOTA, paired superiority over single-run comparators, or isolation
  of temporal specificity from generic trainable-residual capacity. Replace the
  author placeholder and verify legal/licensing fields before publication.
